From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:35:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 241/242] ntdll: count audio underruns and name a stream's
 producer thread

In RDR2's cabin the ml1065 line showed slot 1 delivering 40-50 % of real
time, but the driver counted no underrun, did not say which thread
produced the stream, and did not time its ReleaseBuffer calls, so the
starvation of the producer was inferred, not measured (PLA-364).

ios_mix_stream now counts, per stream while it is started, its render
callbacks, those that found fewer frames than they needed, and the
stream frames missing. Unless MADEIRA_NO_DIAGNOSTICS is set (the host
app's release build):

- the ml1065 line adds the stream, the window's length, the frames
  written and their share of real time, the callbacks, short callbacks
  and missing frames in the window, and the longest gap between two
  ReleaseBuffers with frames;
- the first GetBuffer of each stream logs a getbuf-thread line: the
  calling Windows process and thread, its pthread and Mach port (its
  [xp-t] and [xp-qos] rows), its Windows priority and base priority, and
  its QoS class. thread_ios.c's ios_current_win_thread reads the ids.

With MADEIRA_NO_DIAGNOSTICS the ml1065 line is as before and the
getbuf-thread line is not printed. What is mixed, refused or reported to
the game is unchanged: the counters are relaxed atomic adds in the
callback, which takes no lock and logs nothing.

Linear: PLA-364
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-rdr2-kk-audio-diagnostics.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/audio_null_ios.c | 78 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 build/ntdll-unix/thread_ios.c     | 17 +++++++
 2 files changed, 91 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/audio_null_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/audio_null_ios.c
